let's bring in the Hall of Famer NFL  Network analyst Kurt Warner who joins us  now a little bit of a shocker there on  Saturday what was your first reaction  Kurt I mean I think it was like everyone  else's I mean I I don't think anybody  saw this coming you know especially at  this age at this time we all assumed  that no matter what happened this year  that he would continue to kind of work  through it so I think we're all  surprised but at the same time when you  hear him having been through different  situations in the league I completely  understand it do you think there's  something else that we're missing here I  don't I really think that the bottom  line with the game is that so many  people get into the game because they  they love the game and then there always  seems to be a time when the other stuff  starts to outweigh the love for the game  you know that the Sunday afternoons  nobody stops loving but it's the  preparation it's the offseason and with  Andrew Luck you know it intensifies with  all the rehab and all the pain and  you're never healthy to be able to just  show up and enjoy what you're doing and  I just think it's it's you know going on  for so long that just like he said I  used to love the game now everything  else seems to outweigh my love for the  game in it and it makes it hard to get  up every week going okay here's my week  I got to go do rehab for two hours and  go through all day and then I got to do  rehab again and you know hopefully by  Sunday I'll be able to play pain-free  and do what I love to do but it's always  in the back of mind or you're always  playing hurt and then you have the  expectations I think of now it's when's  he gonna be back out there he needs to  be back out there this team needs and it  seems a championship type team and the  pressure of going I'm still not healthy  what the heck do I do now you know do I  go and play anyways even though I know  I'm not a hundred percent or do I let  this thing kind of play out and then I  hear everybody saying well he should be  out there why is he not out there I see  him doing drills and doing this he looks  like he's good enough to be out there I  just think it weighs on your mind you  know for so long and it's been going on  you know for a number of years now that  I think he's just kind of like I'm tired  of dealing with all the other stuffs  more than I'm dealing with actually  playing and doing what I love doing what  I don't understand I don't know if you  can help me understand this but you he  just it feels like he made an abrupt  decision here now I know he's a thought  out guide deep thinker you know two  weeks ago he talked about he he got  depressed going through all this rehab  that was the first that was the light  that went on for me when I went oh wow  okay I didn't expect to hear that from  him and then when he said that I thought  all right but he's healthy now or  healthier now good offensive line Super  Bowl contender so something it feels  like happen for you to make a decision  that feels like you made a snap judgment  here yeah I mean I understand exactly  what you're saying because I think a lot  of times we have those feelings as you  said it comes to a point where like I  I'm just gonna retire and then you got  to take some time and really think about  it and think about the long term and  it's just really what I want four or  five years from now and not be playing  this game that I love but I have to  believe that you know even though he  said he really kind of sat down and  thought about it I had to believe this  was weighing on his mind for a long  period of time and I think maybe you  know you get two weeks to the season and  everybody's expecting you to play and I  wonder if that plays into it a little  bit as well like I don't think I'm gonna  be out there for week one and you know I  don't want to have to tell everybody you  know I know how long it's going to go on  and we're going week to week that you  just kind of go I'm just going to retire  and let the team move on and move  forward and I'll kind of get some  closure on this and being able to step  away from it but I think it does lend  itself you guys we're talking about your  you know your poll question I think it  does lend itself to okay if you made a  snap decision and it's because you're  not feeling good right now you're only  29 years old does it really open up the  door for 12 months from now when you  actually feel really good and know you  can still play this game to try to come  back and play and and what does that  mean if you go about it this way  talking to hall-of-famer Kurt Warner you  can see him every Sunday on NFL  Network's NFL gameday morning at 9:00  a.m. Eastern starting September 8 I'm  curious in you being in Arizona this  whole clapping with  Kyler's Marie and and the Cardinals what  what am I missing here that they're  doing something illegal I don't think  you're missing anything you know I  actually got a video from their their  media director just yesterday and it was  comparing things that other quarterbacks  have been doing the last couple years  with clapping and kind of the gyrations  back here on the shotgun to what kind of  memory did in the preseason game that  got called for and his is is way less  than what some of these other guys were  doing Sam Donal to josh allen and so i  was with you i went back and watched the  tape over and over again going okay what  am I missing here and then they actually  got called and it was actually Brett  Hundley but he got a call from Blake  I made this past weekend I mean he just  lifted his leg nothing I don't know what  we're missing if they're just trying to  make a point like hey this is new this  is different you know we're going to be  very cautious with this and not let you  do anything but from what I've seen up  to at this point it seems like they're  being targeted a little bit because  they're kind of in the forefront with  this but I don't see anything that you  know I can't believe they're going to  continue to call in the regular season  what they've been calling in the  preseason what if what have you seen  from Kyle Emery I like Tyler you know  but out to practice you know watched all  the games you know the biggest thing for  me is I think he needs to get better or  this offense needs to be better at  handling the Blitz there seems to be a  number of times it gets Minnesota and  against Oakland where they were bringing  pressure and he either didn't have an  answer or he wasn't ready with the  answer against the pressure and they've  got it they better figure that out or  that's gonna be a problem but I think  you saw yesterday there was three or  four just big-time throws from Kyle  Avery I think he's in control he  understands that the moments not too big  I really like him I'm not sure they have  the pieces around him right now for him  to be everything he's going to be but  he's not my biggest concern by any means  with with the Cardinals this year well  that leads me to this question about  putting him in there with an inferior  line that they didn't improve upon last  year and now I'm gonna put him out there  the last thing I want is my rookie  quarterback  go out there and lose confidence be  gun-shy and always be looking you know  that ghosts out there they should he be  starting week one given that offensive  line yes he should be because they're  moving forward to the future and Brett  Hundley is not any part of that and so  yeah I think he should be starting and I  understand your point and I think a big  part of that is always knowing who your  quarterback is what kind of confidence  he has if he goes through some struggles  do you think that's gonna affect him  long-term and you know I think you have  to know that first and foremost and  everything I've heard and everything in  my conversations with Tyler I don't  worry about that I don't look at a guy  that's going to get done shy at any  point time he's a guy that believes he  can make every play he believes he's the  best player on the field Andrew Luck was  another guy he got you know beat up a  lot obviously it's paying some bad  dividends now for the team but he got  beat up a lot when he was young and he  never got gunshot he never shrunk from  that and I don't think Kyle Emery is  that kind of guy but I think it's  important that the organization know who  that quarterback is when they put him in  and that's why I fully believe he should  be the starter week one regardless of  what they have around him and you might  take your lumps early but it's going to  pay dividends for him and for this team  in a long run what would you do with  Daniel Jones with the Giants well I mean  I think you again I said there's a  number of times I think Eli's earned the  right to play himself out of the  position and so I know Daniel has played  well in the preseason but this is Eli's  job and it deserves to be his job until  he shows that he's not the better  quarterback come regular season and when  you're seeing real defenses and when  that point time comes I think it will be  tough to figure out the right timing and  how to do it but I think eli holds the  job this entire year until the  organization is fully believes that  Daniel Jones is the better quarterback  and I'm still not sure that's the case  right now who's your sneaky team this  year there's always one or two that move  up and one or two that moved down  that's a good question you know I mean  and again it's what are you what do you  base it off of I mean you know the two  teams that I think are gonna make big  jumps this year are Atlanta in Minnesota  and again I don't know if you look at  them and go oh they're sneaky because I  mean you know Minnesota's got everything  you know they've got to be a playoff  team this year in Atlanta I mean they  went through so many injuries last year  but their offense  you should be dynamic and as long as  they're decent on defense they should  make a move and you know be in the  playoffs this year as well and so those  are kind of mighty that are on the  outside that I'm looking at and going  they've got to make a run and be much  better than they were record wise last  year is it time for Tennessee to move on  for Marcus Mariota I think it's time to  be on a short leash as much as I like  Marcus as a guy they're just not the  consistency there and now you've got a  guy that has started in this league  behind him that I think you have to see  more consistency week in and week out or  you do have to make the move because you  know I mean this is a year it's either  you're signing into the long franchise  deal or you're not and you know if  you're already convinced he's your guy  than I am and I don't know why you  brought in Ryan Tannehill but you have  to believe they don't believe that right  now and if he doesn't come out and show  that consistency I think you got to  figure out if the other guy is that guy  and and move forward Kurt great to talk  to you we appreciate it and look forward  to those Sunday mornings all right buddy  that's Kurt Warner NFL Network the  Sunday morning show with Rich Eisen NFL  gameday morning at 9:00 a.m. Eastern  starting September 8 for more Dan  Patrick show tune in to audience Channel  239 on DirecTV stream for free on BR  live or download the Dan Patrick show  app  [Music]

